QUESTION_TEXT:
Which Factors affect the Cost of the Car?
Often, motorists begin to think about the technical condition of the vehicle immediately before the sale, which does not in the best sense affect the final price of a car. Those who from the very beginning take care of their swallow significantly benefit in price. In this article, we will consider factors affecting the cost of a car.

It is a mistake to assume that only the year of manufacture and the external condition affect the value of the car. Criteria that you should pay attention to before setting the price of a car:

Car model;
Transmission;
Drive unit;
Auto color;
Electronics;
Additional technologies;
Appearance;
Interior Condition;
Technical condition;
Mileage;
Originality of the TCP.
These are the factors determining the final cost of a vehicle.


Like it or not, but the brand of the car is an important moment in the formation of the cost of a car carzaamin(.)com when it is sold. The brand reflects the main quality of a car - reliability. For example, Japanese cars (Honda, Mazda, Subaru, Toyota) during the first three years lose 65% in value, as well as some English and German models. At the same time, for certain cars the price decreases much more slowly. Such as Infiniti, Acura, Mercedes, Audi and Lexus are valued for several years - in the first 3 years the price drops by no more than 35%.
